---
layout: null
sitemap: false
---
{%- assign docs = site.posts | concat: site.archive | sort: "date" | reverse -%}
[
{%- for doc in docs -%}
{
"t": {{ doc.title | strip_html | strip_newlines | strip | jsonify }},
"u": {{ doc.url | relative_url | jsonify }},
"d": {{ doc.date | date: "%Y-%m-%d" | jsonify }},
"c": {{ doc.categories | join: " " | jsonify }},
{%- comment -%}
Index the full body, not a prefix. Every archive post opens with the same
table-of-contents boilerplate, so a short truncation indexes almost nothing but
that boilerplate. The whole corpus is only ~40k words and the index is fetched
lazily, so the cost is small.
{%- endcomment -%}
"b": {{ doc.content | strip_html | replace: "	", " " | strip_newlines | jsonify }}
}{%- unless forloop.last -%},{%- endunless -%}
{%- endfor -%}
]
